# Route grammar fixture: the wildcard shapes every httpx adapter accepts or
# rejects at registration time (httpx.ValidateWildcardPath).
#
# Source of truth: httpx. protoc-gen-sphere keeps a byte-identical copy
# (generate/http/testdata/golden/route_grammar.golden); change httpx first,
# then copy the file verbatim. The fixture pins the grammar only, not what an
# adapter does with a valid route at run time.
#
# Format: one case per line, "<verdict> <category> <path>", separated by
# single spaces. Lines starting with '#' and blank lines are ignored.
#   verdict   valid | invalid
#   category  ok                    no wildcard, or one named final wildcard
#             not-segment-start     '*' does not begin its own path segment
#             not-final             wildcard is followed by more segments
#             multiple              more than one wildcard in the final segment
#             anonymous             bare '*' with no name
valid ok /
valid ok /health
valid ok /users/:id
valid ok /users/:id/posts/:post
valid ok /files/*name
valid ok /files/*filepath
valid ok /a/b/c/*rest
valid ok /*all
invalid anonymous /files/*
invalid anonymous /*
invalid not-segment-start /foo*bar
invalid not-segment-start /files/pre*name
invalid not-segment-start *name
invalid not-final /a/*x/b
invalid not-final /a/*rest/
invalid not-final /a/*x/b/*y
invalid multiple /a/**
invalid multiple /a/*x*y
